/-!
# Commutator propagation along a regular critical path

The completed results are MS93 (4.4.3), the fixed-core intersection transport,
and the actual neighboring edge required by (4.4.4). Source defines the
terminal subgroup needed for the remaining prescribed-span escape proof.
SourceCriticalApplications proves the b>6 bound and constructs that literal
terminal seed using only the earlier critical-prefix exclusion. Its actual
terminal contradiction also discharges the displacement calculation;
backward-edge switching remains a separate source obligation.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), printed pp.893--894.
-/
